<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seto, Aichi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seto is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aichi-prefecture">Aichi Prefecture</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagoya">Nagoya</a>, which has been a leading centre of pottery for about a thousand years. Its glazed wares were so widespread that setomono, 'Seto things', became a general Japanese word for ceramics. Under the Tokugawa it lay in the Owari Domain, whose lords supported and regulated the kilns.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seto-aichi.jpg" alt="Seto, Aichi" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bariston · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joukouji9.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
